Falsifies `non_volatile_memory_express::verification::admin_queue_attributes_round_trip_the_two_sizes`.

The defect: `admin_queue_attributes` writes the completion count as it stands instead of minus
one. The submission size still decodes and passes, but the controller reads a completion ring one
slot deeper than the driver built, so it writes its last entry of each lap past the ring and the
two sides disagree on where the phase flips.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(((attributes >> 16) & 0xfff) + 1, completion_entries as u32)`.

diff --git a/src/configuration.rs b/src/configuration.rs
--- a/src/configuration.rs
+++ b/src/configuration.rs
@@ -102,7 +102,7 @@
         (2..=4096).contains(&submission_entries) && (2..=4096).contains(&completion_entries),
         "an admin queue holds 2 to 4096 entries"
     );
-    (completion_entries as u32 - 1) << 16 | (submission_entries as u32 - 1)
+    (completion_entries as u32) << 16 | (submission_entries as u32 - 1)
 }
 
 #[cfg(test)]
